,"issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nv4.4.1.stable.arch_linux\nv4.3.stable - Windows 10.0.26100\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.1.stable unknown - Arch Linux #1 SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Fri, 09 May 2025 17:36:18 +0000 on Tty - X11 display driver, Single-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated AMD Radeon RX 7700 XT (RADV NAVI32) - AMD Ryzen 5 7600X 6-Core Processor (12 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nCreating a Sprite2D/MeshInstance2D sized to match a texture with an odd pixel size dimension and with transform position set to integer values renders incorrectly. Shifting it up by a small amount or rounding the vertex in a shader fixes it. Snap 2d pixels to vertices renders it correctly but does shifts everything down by a pixel instead.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/91c4cd14-88a2-49a3-8c8e-670e88bd7788)\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nCreate a Sprite2D with a texture with an odd sized dimension, set the position of the dimension with an odd size to a whole number, and texture filtering to nearest.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[pixel.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20274253/pixel.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https:/